{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778554379,"nonce":"ulMTkSCN9JJKVugfvRpD6nPqUFA=","title":"Downgrade conversation-ID auth match from channel event to passive log","message":"Refines 6d7411b (conversation_id matching for auth event delivery).\n\nCurrently, when conversation_id matches but target_session_id does not, dispatchEvent delivers a full channel event and calls markDelivered — identical to a session_id match. This is wrong when the same conversation is resumed in two different sessions that diverge: both would get channel event wake-ups for each others auth requests.\n\nconversation_id match should be treated as lower confidence than session_id match. The same conversation resumed in two sessions may be doing different work. A full channel event wake-up for a non-matching session is noisy and confusing.\n\nDesign — dispatchEvent tiers:\n1. target_session_id matches ownSessionId -\u003e channel event + markDelivered (unchanged, full confidence)\n2. conversation_id matches ownConversationId but target_session_id does not -\u003e passive log via sendNotification with qualifying context. NO markDelivered (leave in inbox for original session). NO channel event (no agent wake-up). Message includes title, branch, status, and note that it was from a previous session.\n3. No match on either -\u003e drop (unchanged)\n4. target_session_id null (unscoped) -\u003e passive log (unchanged, from 210ffa1)\n5. ownSessionId null -\u003e passive log (unchanged, from 210ffa1)\n\nImplementation: channel-server/notifications.ts dispatchEvent — change the conversation_id branch from deliverAuth()+onDelivered() to sendNotification() with a descriptive message.\n\nTests: Update inbox-scoping.test.ts — existing conversation_id match test should verify sendNotification (not sendChannelEvent) and NO onDelivered. Add test confirming notification message contains qualifying \"previous session\" language.","files":null}]}